WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:09.000
Tesla renamed its driver assistant system in Europe to Tesla-assisted driving after years of regulatory criticism over the prior label. This is Tesla Shorts Time,

00:00:09.520 --> 00:00:26.620
Episode 630. Tesla's 3rd quarter earnings report lands on October 21. Market Beat has posted the consensus estimates for that quarter. In China, the cybercab went on display at Suzhaum Mixi World. The post from TSMMing described massive local buzz around the vehicle.

00:00:26.620 --> 00:00:30.580
The same account noted the atmosphere at the event felt super exciting.

00:00:31.320 --> 00:00:34.520
Tesla changed the name of its driver assistance system across Europe.

00:00:35.160 --> 00:00:38.820
German and other European sites now listed as Tesla-assisted driving.

00:00:39.340 --> 00:00:43.780
The old full-self driving supervise label had drawn years of regulatory criticism.

00:00:44.400 --> 00:00:47.920
Tesla once dropped the autopilot name after earlier legal fights.

00:00:48.280 --> 00:00:52.320
The company kept the full-self driving supervise name inside the United States.

00:00:53.340 --> 00:00:57.440
NHTSA's scrutiny continues over the Robotaxi design that lacks a brake pedal.

00:00:57.960 --> 00:01:01.300
Tesla introduced an emergency drive-away feature at Superchargers.

00:01:01.800 --> 00:01:05.020
Drivers can now shift into drive while the cable stays attached.

00:01:05.540 --> 00:01:09.500
The company warns this can cause up to $25,000 in charger damage.

00:01:10.140 --> 00:01:12.900
A mandatory vehicle service visit follows every use.

00:01:13.500 --> 00:01:16.560
The feature works at V2, V3, and V4 stalls.

00:01:17.060 --> 00:01:18.640
It does not work at home chargers.

00:01:18.640 --> 00:01:22.740
The rollout came after a shooting at a supercharger in Twin Falls, Idaho.

00:01:23.420 --> 00:01:26.700
Tesla confirmed glycol coolant would spill and require cleanup.

00:01:27.200 --> 00:01:30.360
Owners asked if emergency use would still bring damage charges.

00:01:30.900 --> 00:01:32.700
Tesla gave no answer on that point.

00:01:33.220 --> 00:01:36.840
The Tesla AI account on X changed its handle to Tesla SI.

00:01:37.340 --> 00:01:40.020
The display name now reads Tesla's superintelligence.

00:01:40.680 --> 00:01:44.560
Elon Musk confirmed a similar move at SpaceX AI on October 4.

00:01:44.560 --> 00:01:49.960
A September 29 executive order pushed federal agencies towards superintelligence wording.

00:01:50.500 --> 00:01:53.920
Elon Musk posted a sarcastic message aimed at Mukesh Ambani.

00:01:54.400 --> 00:01:57.140
He called the Reliance Chairman Prime Minister Ambani.

00:01:57.760 --> 00:02:02.320
Musk accused Ambani of monopolistic exploitation and asked if Starlink could compete.

00:02:02.900 --> 00:02:05.940
Starlink has spent five years meeting Indian government rules.

00:02:06.480 --> 00:02:11.040
Three companies already hold SATCOM licenses while spectrum pricing stays undecided.

00:02:11.040 --> 00:02:14.480
It must highlight its Starlink's role during natural disasters.

00:02:14.900 --> 00:02:18.120
The Indian government called claims of unfair rules baseless.

00:02:18.600 --> 00:02:22.160
In Australia, Tesla cut prices on and stock Model 3 vehicles.

00:02:22.700 --> 00:02:27.740
Buyers in ACT, TAS and Victoria see up to $2,750 off.

00:02:28.300 --> 00:02:32.280
A $2,000 trade in bonus stays available through the end of 2026.

00:02:32.940 --> 00:02:37.640
The new Model 3 RWD starts at $45,900 before on roads.

00:02:37.640 --> 00:02:42.340
modes. That variant carries a 572 kilometer WLTP range.

00:02:42.860 --> 00:02:51.000
Tesla sold 41,705 EVs in Australia through September. 5,775 of those sales were Model

00:02:51.000 --> 00:02:57.260
3's. The Powerwall 3 in Japan carries flood resistance up to 0.6 meters. The certification

00:02:57.260 --> 00:03:03.420
appears on the Tesla Japan site. A California buyer purchased a new 2026 Model X plaid

00:03:03.420 --> 00:03:05.740
for $118,880.

00:03:06.280 --> 00:03:09.320
After 7,000 miles, the owner sold it at a profit.

00:03:09.980 --> 00:03:11.860
Tesla posted that floodgates are opening

00:03:11.860 --> 00:03:13.880
in reference to cybercabs and traffic.

00:03:14.420 --> 00:03:17.080
The message came from the official Tesla account on X.

00:03:17.580 --> 00:03:20.860
A Model S plaid reached 204 miles per hour in testing.

00:03:21.420 --> 00:03:23.500
The post from Tesla Roddy noted excitement

00:03:23.500 --> 00:03:24.800
for the upcoming Roadster.

00:03:25.400 --> 00:03:27.240
Halloween mode does not work on vehicles

00:03:27.240 --> 00:03:28.480
