00:04:05.620 --> 00:04:11.360
Construction continues on Tesla's Arizona energy complex. Tesla signed a deal covering 90%

00:04:11.360 --> 00:04:16.920
of the site's output. Footage shows a passenger unable to stop or exit a cyber cab during repeated

00:04:16.920 --> 00:04:22.200
loops. The incident points to unresolved control questions in early unsupervised operation.

00:04:22.820 --> 00:04:28.240
Tesla has not commented publicly on the specific event. Battery flood resistance ratings rest

00:04:28.240 --> 00:04:33.080
on enclosure ceiling and internal component isolation rather than overall pack capacity.

00:04:33.620 --> 00:04:39.720
A Powerwall 3 certified to 0.6 meters must maintain electrical isolation even when water reaches

00:04:39.720 --> 00:04:45.360
that height. This engineering choice adds cost at the component level but reduces insurance and

00:04:45.360 --> 00:04:50.520
liability exposure for owners and flood prone regions. The same ceiling approach interacts with

00:04:50.520 --> 00:04:55.820
installation height requirements. Installers must still position the unit above expected water lines

00:04:55.820 --> 00:05:01.300
and many jurisdictions. The certified rating gives a measurable safety margin when local codes lag

00:05:01.300 --> 00:05:06.800
behind product capability. For Tesla Energy, the incremental ceiling investment supports a broader

00:05:06.800 --> 00:05:12.580
residential storage strategy that pairs Powerwall units with solar and virtual power plant programs.

00:05:13.080 --> 00:05:17.840
Higher weather resilience expands the addressable customer base without requiring separate product

00:05:17.840 --> 00:05:23.480
variants. Before we go, watch for more details on the Arizona Energy Complex output deal,

00:05:23.480 --> 00:05:26.240
And that's everything worth knowing about Tesla today.

